Director, HR Operational Excellence and Compliance

YOUR TASKS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

The primary responsibilities of this role, Director, Human Resources Operational Excellence and Compliance are to:

The Director, HR Operational Excellence and Compliance will lead North America-wide governance, execution, and modernization across critical HR compliance, immigration, onboarding, and other Talent Acquisition compliance processes. The role strengthens Bayer's License to Operate by ensuring disciplined execution while building a more scalable operating model that uses clear ownership, AI agents, automation, knowledge management, external partners, and fit-for-purpose outsourcing models.

This leader will be expected to move beyond issue management and become the organizing force for a future-state North America support model, including progressive evolution of Canadian support, stronger TA compliance and onboarding controls, improved service expectations, and practical deployment of AI-enabled support that reduces manual work while preserving compliance, privacy, and employee trust.

North America Compliance Governance, ERISA & Regulatory Stewardship

- Lead North America-wide HR compliance governance across U.S. and Canadian support structures, with accountability for execution, risk visibility, and sustainable operating discipline;
- Oversee critical compliance domains including ERISA governance, regulatory body interactions, SOP and Internal Control System expectations, audit readiness, I-9 management, reasonable accommodations, HR investigations, immigration, talent mobility, and TA/onboarding compliance controls;
- Establish governance forums and decision frameworks that clarify accountability across HR, Talent Acquisition, Payroll, Benefits, Legal, Finance, Tax, Operations, Digital, and external partner interfaces;
- Strengthen preventive and detective controls across federal, state, provincial, and local requirements, ensuring that compliance work is documented, assigned, measurable, and resilient;
- Serve as a trusted advisor during internal and external audits and help establish consistent audit response frameworks;
- Identify control gaps, process fragmentation, ownership ambiguity, and single points of failure; drive sustainable remediation plans.

Execution Leadership, Team Organization & Operating Model Design

- Own delivery of priority initiatives while organizing the team, routines, escalation paths, documentation, and decision rights needed to support ongoing compliance enablement work at scale;
- Design a future-state resource model that blends core internal expertise, AI-enabled agents, workflow tools, shared services, external vendors, and outsourcing support where appropriate;
- Improve service quality and scalability through clear SLAs, intake standards, change control, governance routines, and vendor/partner accountability, including Ruveon-related change control expectations;
- Lead progressive evolution of Canadian support to ensure the North America model is integrated where appropriate while respecting country-specific compliance, employment, privacy, and operational differences;
- Strengthen documentation standards, knowledge management practices, and cross-training expectations across critical compliance processes;
- Partner with functional owners to transition selected operational activities into Payroll and Benefits where ownership more naturally aligns.

AI Agents, Automation, Outsourcing & Digital Enablement

- Lead practical deployment of AI agents, automation, workflow technology, analytics, and knowledge tools to improve compliance execution, employee support, TA/onboarding experiences, and operational decision-making;
- Identify work that should remain internally owned versus work that can be supported through outsourced resources, managed services, vendors, or AI-enabled self-service models;
- Partner with HR Technology, Workday, Paradox, Ruveon, Payroll, Benefits, Legal, Digital, TA Operations, and Operational Excellence teams to design scalable, governed, and user-centered solutions;
- Apply emerging AI capabilities to improve process documentation, knowledge management, risk identification, employee support, and operational decision support;
- Promote responsible experimentation with AI and automation while maintaining appropriate governance, privacy, data quality, and compliance discipline;
- Build a culture of curiosity, continuous learning, and practical innovation around future-of-work capabilities.

Core Domain Accountability

- ERISA compliance, regulatory body coordination, SOP governance, Internal Control System discipline, and audit-ready documentation;
- I-9 management for Talent Acquisition, TA and Paradox-related reasonable accommodations, onboarding controls, and service delivery issue resolution;
- HR investigations, immigration, talent mobility, SLA governance, change control, and vendor/resource model effectiveness.

Cross-Functional Leadership

- Partner closely with Payroll, Benefits, HR Business Partners, Legal, Finance, Tax, Internal Audit, and external vendors or advisors;
- Influence stakeholders across a complex matrix environment without relying solely on formal authority;
- Facilitate alignment across multiple functions involved in compliance-related activities and controls;
- Lead governance forums, stakeholder discussions, and executive-ready updates on compliance priorities, operational risk, and modernization of progress;
- Translate complex compliance, audit, and process topics into clear recommendations and practical action plans.

Workforce Capability & Organizational Resilience

- Develop and implement strategies that reduce single points of failure across critical compliance work;
- Establish knowledge transfer, documentation, and cross-training plans for critical processes and stakeholder relationships;
- Coach leaders and teams on compliance ownership, governance expectations, audit readiness, and operating discipline;
- Support organizational transformation as North America HR Foundations evolves its operating model and modernizes service delivery.

WHO YOU ARE

Bayer seeks an incumbent who possesses the following:

Required Qualifications:

- Significant progressive leadership experience in HR Compliance, HR Operations, Talent Acquisition Operations, Immigration/Talent Mobility, Payroll, Benefits, Risk Management, Governance, Operational Excellence, or related disciplines;
- Demonstrated success leading director-level operating model transformation, cross-functional governance, resource model design, outsourcing/vendor strategy, and execution of complex enterprise initiatives;
- Strong understanding of U.S. HR compliance requirements and governance frameworks; ability to learn and navigate cross-border U.S./Canada implications;
- Working knowledge of ERISA/DOL governance, pension and savings plan oversight, Form 5500 processes, SPD controls, employment tax interfaces, I-9 governance, and regulatory audit management;
- Experience partnering with Legal, Audit, Tax, Payroll, Benefits, Finance, HR Operations, and external advisors;
- Strong analytical, problem-solving, and systems-thinking capabilities;
- Excellent executive communication, stakeholder management, facilitation, and influencing skills;
- Comfort operating in ambiguity and leading through change in a matrixed environment.

Preferred Qualifications:

- Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Finance, Legal Studies, Public Policy, Risk Management, Organizational Effectiveness, or a related field; advanced degree preferred.
- Experience supporting both U.S. and Canadian HR compliance environments;
- Experience with Workday or comparable HR technology ecosystems;
- Experience applying Lean, Six Sigma, Operational Excellence, Process Management, Design Thinking, or similar methodologies;
- Experience implementing automation, workflow tools, analytics, AI-enabled solutions, or digital process improvements;
- Vendor governance or external advisor management experience.
- Formation leadership.

